============================================================================================
SUMMARY (data-grounded)
============================================================================================
HIGHEST MILLENNIUM (R1 mean criterion): 4000-3001 BCE (= CE -4000..-3001 = 4951-5950 calBP), mean Amber_inter = 1.488, next best usable block -0.277, gap 1.77 Z.
PEAK INTERVAL: core (top-decile bins & Z=1.54 platform) 3300..2901 BCE (5251-4851 calBP);
             broad high plateau (mean+1SD / half-max, all levels >= 1.46) 4000..2901 BCE (5951-4851 calBP).
SMOOTHED PEAK POSITION: 3275-3175 BCE depending on window (50-250 y), band ~2900-4100 BCE.
UNCERTAINTY: +/-100 y (one century bin); sub-century ordering of the 1.46 and 1.54 plateaux is NOT resolvable.
PROXY CAVEAT: no price/value field exists; Z = standardised find abundance/density -> relative
  importance/circulation only; frequency != value. High-positive = more amber is a CONVENTION.
